! v1.10.2 ladder STEP 5, part 2 of 2: the Cheng-Evans-Van Voorhis
! constraint-release protocol on the symmetric pair.
!
! The reference SCF is the Becke-weight CDFT with +0.05 forced onto
! H1; at t = 0 the constraint is RELEASED (the RT Fock simply omits
! the constraint potential) and the polarization charge oscillates
! between the atoms.  ORACLE: the beat of q_H1(t) must equal
! 2 |H_AB(GMH)| = 0.930653 Ha (the companion GMH run).  Observed:
!   dt = 0.2:  0.93251 Ha   (dt^2 propagator phase error)
!   dt = 0.1:  0.93090 Ha   (+0.027 % from 2 H_AB)  <- this test
! Amplitude systematics checked separately: +0.02 and +0.10
! constraints shift the beat by < 0.03 % (mean-field anharmonicity).
! The t = 0 self-check E(0) = E_scf HOLDS (3e-12): the CDFT module
! reports the physical E_KS at the constrained density, exactly what
! the released (unconstrained) Fock reproduces.  Field-free release
! conserves E to 1.9e-9 Ha over 12000 steps.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%scf_ptol 1e-9
%cdft    becke
Hplus   1  charge  +0.05
%cdft_tol 1.0e-7
%rt_tddft 12000
%rt_dt    0.1
%rt_print_every 2000
%rt_pc_maxiter 4
%geom angstrom
H  0.0 0.0 0.0
H  0.0 0.0 0.74
*end
